course: dictionary
lesson: 12088
title: Clubhouse
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A clubhouse is a building where a club meets. Sports clubs such as golf, tennis, rugby, cricket and sailing clubs often have one, with changing rooms, a meeting room and a café.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «The golf players had lunch in the clubhouse after their game.» Golf players, lunch and a game all point to a place where a club gathers, so clubhouse must mean a club building.
explain: Children can have a clubhouse too. It is a den or small hut used as a secret club place, a bit like a treehouse. «We built a secret clubhouse in the old oak tree.» Secret tells you the clubhouse is a hidden place for a club.
fact: A clubhouse is a building used by a sports club or other club.
fact: A clubhouse often has changing rooms, a meeting room or a café.
fact: A clubhouse can also be a den or small hut that children use as a secret club place.
fact: Golf, tennis, rugby, cricket and sailing clubs often have a clubhouse where members meet and change.
fact: Some children make rules for their clubhouse, such as «No grown-ups allowed».
exercise: «The golf players had lunch in the clubhouse after their game.» Where did they have lunch? | Under a tree in the rain | At the bottom of the sea | *In the clubhouse, the building used by the golf club | In the car park
exercise: Sara says a clubhouse is always a big house with a swimming pool. What is a clubhouse really? | *A building or small hut used as a club meeting place | A bus stop by the river | A shop that sells only sports balls | A large house for one family
exercise: «We built a secret clubhouse in the old oak tree.» Find the word that tells you the clubhouse is hidden from other people. | *secret | built | tree | oak
test: «No grown-ups allowed» is a rule some children write for their clubhouse. What does this tell you? | It is a hospital for sports players | *It can be a secret club place that children use | It is always a shop for grown-ups | It is a place where grown-ups must always stay
test: Which place would most likely be called a clubhouse? | A hospital ward for sick people | A railway station with trains and ticket offices | A school library full of books | *A tennis club's building with changing rooms and a café
exam: Which sentence explains the word clubhouse best? | *A clubhouse is a building or den used as a club meeting place | A clubhouse is a sports ball made of rubber | A clubhouse is a type of bird that lives near water | A clubhouse is a rope used for climbing trees
